{
  "_help": [
	"Pets (Bound Souls): scripts/PetDb.cs reads this file; Cube.cs throws Soul Cubes, Pet.cs is the world companion, UiPets.cs the menu (P).",
	"Every enemy type in data/enemies.json is catchable. Species data is derived from the enemy def (rarity from hp / boss flag, element from dmgType,",
	"  pet scale from the body height) and can be overridden here under \"species\" or in enemies.json as \"catch\": { rarity, base, archetype, skills, mountable, petScale, mountScale }.",
	"  Shades (shade / shadeArcher / shadeCaster) are mirror copies of heroes (Enemy.ShadeOf) and are listed in \"uncatchable\".",
	"Catch chance = rarity base x hpFactor x statusBonus x levelGap x cube multiplier (bossMul for bosses and raid bosses), clamped to [minChance or bossMinChance, maxChance].",
	"  hpFactor = hpFloor + (1 - hpFloor) x (1 - hp%)^hpCurve.  levelGap = clamp(1 - levelGapPer x (foe level - hero level), levelGapMin, levelGapMax).",
	"  The cube shakes up to 3 times; each shake passes with chance^(1/3), so all three pass with exactly the catch chance.",
	"Skills: world fields (range m, cd s, fx melee/bolt/breath/nova/self) and turn-based fields for Soul Duels (power, acc %, cost = focus points, priority, effect + chance + turns).",
	"  kind: attack | heal (power = % of max hp) | shield (guard: damage taken x0.5) | buff (atk x buffMul) | debuff (status on foes around).",
    "Stats (duel numbers): stat = (a x enemy field + b) x (1 + perLevel x (level - 1)) x nature x rarity statMul, plus gear. World combat floors pet hp / damage to a share of the hero's (stats.world)."
  ],
